{"id":"eta-residual-evaluation","t":"Evaluate ETA predictions by segment","tags":["Regression","Metrics & Evaluation"],"d":"Easy","rt":"numpy","fn":"eta_report","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"Write `eta_report(pred, actual, segment, late_tol)` for trip time predictions in minutes.\n\nFor each segment (sorted by name) and for `\"ALL\"` last, report:\n\n- `n`\n- `mae`: mean absolute error\n- `mape`: mean of $|pred - actual| / actual$ over trips with `actual > 0`, or `nan` if none\n- `bias`: mean of `pred - actual` (negative means the app promises too early)\n- `late_rate`: fraction of trips where `actual > pred + late_tol`, the trips that arrived later than promised beyond the tolerance\n- `p90_abs`: `np.percentile(abs error, 90)`\n\nReturn a dict from segment name to a dict of these values.","starter":"import numpy as np\n\ndef eta_report(pred, actual, segment, late_tol):\n    \"\"\"Per-segment ETA error report.\"\"\"\n    e = np.abs(np.asarray(pred) - np.asarray(actual))\n    return {\"ALL\": {\"n\": len(e), \"mae\": float(e.mean())}}\n","hints":["Write one helper that computes all metrics for a pair of arrays, then call it per segment and once for everything.","Late rate is one-sided: a trip that arrives early is not late, however large the error."],"sol":"import numpy as np\n\ndef _stats(p, a, tol):\n    d = p - a\n    pos = a > 0\n    return {\"n\": int(len(p)), \"mae\": float(np.abs(d).mean()),\n            \"mape\": float((np.abs(d[pos]) / a[pos]).mean()) if pos.any() else float(\"nan\"),\n            \"bias\": float(d.mean()), \"late_rate\": float((a > p + tol).mean()),\n            \"p90_abs\": float(np.percentile(np.abs(d), 90))}\n\ndef eta_report(pred, actual, segment, late_tol):\n    p, a, g = np.asarray(pred, float), np.asarray(actual, float), np.asarray(segment)\n    out = {str(s): _stats(p[g == s], a[g == s], late_tol) for s in sorted(set(g.tolist()))}\n    out[\"ALL\"] = _stats(p, a, late_tol)\n    return out\n","ex_md":"## Why more than MAE\nUsers judge ETAs asymmetrically. Arriving five minutes early is pleasant; arriving five minutes late after a promise is a complaint. Bias and late rate measure that directly, and a model with lower MAE but a negative bias can be worse for the product.\n\n## Why segment\nAn overall metric hides groups where the model fails, such as airport trips with long waits at pick-up or rush-hour city trips. Reporting by segment is how you find the slice that needs a feature or a separate correction.\n\n## Tail errors\nThe 90th percentile of absolute error tracks the bad experiences that drive churn; MAE can improve while the tail gets worse.\n\n## Interview follow-ups\n- Should the model be trained on a loss that matches this asymmetry, such as a quantile loss?","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"[10, 20, 30]\n[12, 18, 40]\n['a', 'b', 'a']\n2.0","out":"{'a': {'n': 2, 'mae': 6.0, 'mape': 0.20833333333333331, 'bias': -6.0, 'late_rate': 0.5, 'p90_abs': 9.2}, 'b': {'n': 1, 'mae': 2.0, 'mape': 0.1111111111111111, 'bias': 2.0, 'late_rate': 0.0, 'p90_abs': 2.0}, 'ALL': {'n': 3, 'mae': 4.666666666666667, 'mape': 0.17592592592592593, 'bias': -3.3333333333333335, 'late_rate': 0.3333333333333333, 'p90_abs': 8.4}}"},{"in":"array([ 6.75438413, 19.35872364, 20.48163368,  4.97863488, 13.77108736,\n       21.64964564, 18.64909063, 20.5314554 , 22.76166948, 27.07049695,\n        2.43749556, 21.46747231, 29.35813732, 15.74724777,  9.17401559,\n       23.72843008, 19.23205862, 23.22375932, 30.77299542, 17.7758412 ,\n        7.56851485, 13.93400369,  8.01080285, 19.78907222, 28.38330156,\n       29.29972312,  4.49427922, 26.87829841, 16.3974369 , 15.66626561,\n       25.91842077,  9.36598255, 32.88734304,  3.34079208, 19.80667829,\n       16.507538  , 26.61832906, 15.00670068, 21.19550578, 11.94210753,\n       12.30937886, 24.0 …\narray([ 7.76277871, 22.36956395, 23.84022289,  7.69464028, 13.20132244,\n       26.2323975 , 20.33088535, 21.6726596 , 23.92276185, 25.10059177,\n        7.26868182, 20.36475125, 35.91